INSERT INTO feature VALUES('signature-models','descriptions','Models of a signature (Model(S))','signatures-as-values','implemented','notable',NULL,'`Model(S)` derives a module type from a signature, one component per sort, operation and rule, checked against an instance; an interface operation runs at its type arguments; it also signs a functor''s parameter. A theory''s `oper x : A`, a type alone after the colon, is a constant of that type, answered by a value member; a thunk type after the colon is the operation it curries, and a port at a builtin type derives. A port that binds variables, `k : pi+ (s : S) . C`, is the thunked function from them, `+U ((s : S) -> -F C)`, the standard model of a second-order signature, so a state-passing module is a model of `State`; a law relating a term at such a port is refused by name (#1324). `Model(T) with sort x = A` fixes a sort of the model type to a type, as a manifest component the members then read. A theory''s `oper x : Model(T)` nests a model of `T`, answered by a submodule ascribed `Model(T)` and sealed with its enclosing model, its sort written as a path through the nested model''s name, `Sealed.inner.T`. `Model(T)` in a type is the bundled record the signature states, node for node the written dependent record (`Σ` over a field a later one names, laws as `Path` fields), so a path between two models is their structure identity read field by field; `pack M` at a manifest `Model(T)` lowers to that record, and a pattern at `Model(T)` opens it. A module''s name read as a value, `M`, is that record at the model type its header ascribes, with no `pack` written; a module no model type ascribes is no value. Where a definition''s signature, a parameter''s type or an annotation asks a module at a manifest model type of its theory, its record leaves out each sort that type fixes, so the module stands there, and a module whose carrier is another type is refused `TypeMismatch` (#4826). `Model(T) with sort x = A` is itself a type, a chain fixing one sort per `with`: the family in `A` takes an equivalence of carriers to a path between the manifest types by `Path.ap`, and `Path.walk` carries a model along it. Each set of unindexed sorts of a theory that a manifest model type of the unit fixes takes one forgetting map, at every carrier, from the theory''s models with those sorts manifest to its models, which puts each carrier back as its field and keeps every other sort the field it is; a manifest model, fixing some sorts or all, stands where a model of its theory is asked, the checker solving the carriers from the model''s type and applying the map there. Beside it, the set takes one map per theory a reduct of the theory restricts to, putting the carriers back and then restricting, so a manifest model of an extension stands where an included theory''s model is asked. A model binder''s sort is a type: `a.C` for `a : Model(T)` is the carrier `a`''s record holds, so a second model fixing its sort to it, `with sort C = a.C`, shares `a`''s carrier; a sort `a`''s type fixes is the type it is fixed to, and one it leaves a field beside a fixed one is that field of the record. An operation is read off a binder alike, a parameter or a `let` written at the model type: `a.op` is the operation `a`''s record holds at its derived type, the carriers read as `a`''s, whether the record nests or is keyed by the operations, and a sort the type fixes is no member a computation reads; `a.op(x)` calls it in place, as `let f = a.op ; f(x)` does. The map is written `forget[sort C = A, …](m) at Model(T)`, naming the sorts it puts back with their carriers as a manifest type binds them, in any order: the call the checker applies at the crossing, which an ascription `(m : Model(T))` states without writing it. The explicit form writes the map the checker applies where each carrier is a type and the map lands on the model''s own theory, the sugared form leaves it to the checker, and hover at the crossing names it; a carrier selected off a binder and a map composed with a reduct stay the checker''s in both forms. A rule''s component is a `Path` in the carrier: `Path.here` witnesses it where the carrier converts the rule''s two sides, and a written path witnesses it otherwise.','surface-lowering core-checker core-term surface-dispatcher','corpus/model/higher-cells/cat-shape.gandr corpus/model/modules/model-ascription.gandr corpus/pathological/modules/model-ascription.gandr corpus/model/modules/model-rule-witnesses.gandr corpus/model/modules/model-functor.gandr corpus/model/modules/model-constant.gandr corpus/model/modules/model-operation.gandr corpus/model/modules/model-manifest.gandr corpus/pathological/modules/model-manifest.gandr corpus/model/modules/model-nested.gandr corpus/pathological/modules/model-nested.gandr corpus/model/identity/model-identity.gandr corpus/model/desc/lc/model-record.gandr corpus/model/identity/model-counter.gandr corpus/model/modules/model-manifest-type.gandr corpus/pathological/modules/model-manifest-type.gandr corpus/model/identity/model-counter-manifest.gandr corpus/pathological/identity/model-counter-manifest.gandr corpus/model/identity/model-counter-manifest-explicit.gandr corpus/pathological/identity/model-counter-manifest-explicit.gandr corpus/model/include/reduct.gandr corpus/pathological/include/reduct.gandr corpus/model/effects/state-model.gandr corpus/pathological/effects/state-model.gandr corpus/model/modules/module-value.gandr corpus/pathological/modules/module-value.gandr crates/surface-lowering/tests/modules/models.rs crates/core-checker-base/src/module/tests.rs crates/core-checker-base/tests/module.rs','corpus/model/higher-cells/cat-shape.gandr','#2203');
